This pull request implements new varieties of the find_duplicates function, both in java and python. There is additional information about these implementations and others in the README.md file. This pull is a part of [this lab assignment.](https://csci338.github.io/fall2024/assignments/lab03)
This code was implemented in two languages:

- Java
```
public static List<Integer> findModeMap(List<Integer> l){
    List<Integer> duplicates = new ArrayList<Integer>();
    Map<Integer, Integer> aux = new HashMap<Integer, Integer>();
    Integer temp;
    for(Integer i : l){
        temp = aux.get(i);
        if(temp == null){
            aux.put(i, i);
        }else{
            duplicates.add(temp);
        }
    }
    return duplicates;
}
```
- Python
```
def find_duplicates_map(l: list) -> list:
    duplicates = []
    aux = set()
    for i in l:
        if i in aux:
            duplicates.append(i)
        else:
            aux.add(i)
    return duplicates
```

